From 0f830125987631a9ce8cde4ed8fc16aa6eb5eb2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nirmal Raj S <nirm@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 15:09:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prevent agent reset caused by MQTT broker keepalive timeout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The slave_wlan_hal connects to the local MQTT broker with a keepalive
of 60 s. The manual mosquitto loop (loop_read + loop_write) was used
without ever calling mosquitto_loop_misc(). That function is responsible
for sending PINGREQ keepalive packets; without it no PINGREQ is ever
sent, the broker disconnects the client after 60 s of silence, the
MQTT socket fd becomes invalid, the event loop fires on_disconnect/
on_error for slave_hal_ext_events, and the agent resets.

Fix:
- mqtt_client.h/cpp: add MQTTClient::ping() which calls
  mosquitto_loop_misc() to send a PINGREQ keepalive packet.
- slave_wlan_hal.h: add virtual send_ping() default no-op to the
  slave_wlan_hal interface.
- slave_wlan_hal_nl80211.h/cpp: override send_ping() with a 30-second
  interval timer (last_ping_time_); calls mqtt_client.ping() when due.
- slave_wlan_hal_dummy/onewifi/whm .h/.cpp: add dummy send_ping()
  no-op overrides for HALs that do not use an MQTT broker.
- son_slave_thread.h/cpp: add send_slave_hal_ping() which delegates to
  m_slave_wlan_hal->send_ping(). fsm_all() calls send_slave_hal_ping() on
  every 200 ms FSM timer tick, guaranteeing a PINGREQ is sent every
  30 s — well within the broker's keepalive * 1.5 = 90 s disconnect
  deadline.

Signed-off-by: Nirmal Raj S <nirm@qti.qualcomm.com>
